      "vision_by": "cloud-subagent:sonnet",
      "vision_reason": "This is a Mesoamerican-style pottery censer/vessel with a modeled anthropomorphic figure wearing a mask, headband, and sandals — a ceramic tradition typical of West Mexico or Veracruz, not the Fang of Gabon; nothing about the object matches Fang material culture (which is known for bieri reliquary figures, bark cloth, and wood carving, not this kind of figural ceramic urn).",
