      "styles": [],
      "categories": [],
      "physical_description": null,
      "summary": "Pottery vessel in the shape of a vase with a (male?) figure modelled at the front, probably a censer. The figure has a beaked nose, small fangs, and seems to be wearing a mask around the eyes and mouth. The figure is wearing a loincloth and tied sandals, as well as earplugs and a headband. Both hands / lower arms are broken off. The vessel is shaped with an incense bowl at the top, which has appliqued circles on the front, above the figure. There are two holes on each side of the main body of the vessel.",
